refs/vendor/bpi-r4pro-8x-openwrt24.10/target/linux/mediatek/files-6.6/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt7988a-bananapi-bpi-r4-pro-8x.dts

Adapted-by: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5) for ImmortalWrt 25.12 /
Linux 6.12.91.

The vendor BPI-R4 Pro 8X hardware uses a GPIO-controlled combo path on
the MxL86252C switch: one user port can be switched between an SFP
channel and a copper PHY channel according to the SFP MOD_DEF0 presence
GPIO.  The upstream-style MxL862xx driver stack imported from OpenWrt PR
#21083 does not include that vendor mux behavior.

Keep the feature optional and device-tree driven.  Boards without a
`ds-mux-bus` child under the MxL switch keep the PR driver behavior
unchanged.  Compared with the vendor implementation, keep the same
hardware semantics but isolate the mux code in a separate translation
unit and harden the DSA/phylink lifetime handling: restore the original
DSA phylink before switch unregister/shutdown, avoid destroying DSA's
base phylink, and roll back on channel switch failure.

